{"kind":"stack","id":"s-env-change","title":"Environments can change and pose dangers to living things","theme":{"background":"#f4f9f1","foreground":"#1d3b2a","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"What is an environment?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a1","label":"Everything around a living thing, including the air, water and land","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a2","label":"Only the animals that live in one place","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a3","label":"Only the plants that grow in a garden","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-term","content":"Environment change"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-expl","content":"When the conditions where living things live become different, for example through weather, floods, fires or people building on land."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"rain"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Heavy rain floods a field. What is the danger to the worms living in the soil?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a1","label":"They can drown when the soil fills with water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a2","label":"They become brighter in colour","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a3","label":"They grow much bigger overnight","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which change to an environment is caused by people?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a1","label":"Cutting down a forest to build houses","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a2","label":"A leaf falling from a tree in autumn","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a3","label":"The Sun rising in the morning","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"A pond in your local park is drying up in a long summer heatwave. The frogs must move. Which path do they take?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a1","label":"Walk to the stream nearby","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a2","label":"Stay in the mud and wait","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"The frogs reach the stream and find cool water. They survive the heatwave."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The mud dries hard and many frogs cannot escape the heat."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Why can a drying pond be dangerous for frogs?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a1","label":"Their water and shelter disappear","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a2","label":"The pond becomes too deep to swim","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a3","label":"The frogs learn to fly","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-term","content":"Habitat"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-expl","content":"The natural home of a living thing, where it finds food, water and shelter."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"A wildfire burns part of a woodland. Which living things are most at risk?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a1","label":"Animals and plants that cannot move away quickly","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a2","label":"Only the rocks on the ground","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a3","label":"Only the clouds in the sky","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the lesson on changing environments."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Environments can change, and living things must adapt or move to stay safe."}],"actions":[]}}
